# Breakthrough-loop discipline (drop into .cursor/rules/)
Full methodology: https://github.com/GuoCheng24/breakthrough-harness

When running research experiments in this project:
- Triage the target first: cheap scoring function + existing groundwork +
  externally recognisable win. Any missing -> flag it and stop.
- Build the harness before the method: single evaluation entry point;
  null models scored first and pinned to the floor; metric conventions pinned
  (double-report if the published one differs); calibration and evaluation
  data physically separated - tuning touches calibration only.
- Reproduce a published baseline number before trusting ours; an unmatched
  baseline means the recipe has unread layers (optimizer, loss, metric
  convention, operator).
- Loop: 10-30 variants/round each with a one-line reason it might win;
  sanity-check before entry; executors only call the entry point, never
  write method code inline; select on calibration; confirm top-k held-out.
  Unreproduced gains do not exist. Persist numbers to disk, then write.
- Claim polarity: the main sentence of any result is constructive
  ("we propose X, it solves Y, number Z"); audits and negatives are
  supporting material, never the headline.
- Verify every new guard by deliberately breaking what it watches, and
  confirm it fails for the right reason.
